by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-12T00:52:01Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T05:05:49Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T01:26:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118438","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118438","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118438.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118438.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #118430\n\n**Race 1: `get_named_pool()` — unsynchronized write to static `named_pools`**\nThe static `named_pools` HashMap was read and written without any mutex. Concurrent calls with new pool names could corrupt the HashMap. Added a dedicated `static BinaryMutex named_pools_mutex` to protect all access.\n\n**Race 2: `wait_for_group_task_completion()` — dangling HashMap internal pointer**\nThe function obtained a `Group**` pointer into the HashMap's internal storage, then released the mutex before dereferencing it. A concurrent insert could trigger a rehash, invalidating the pointer. Now the `Group*` is copied under the lock, avoiding reliance on HashMap internals after the lock is released.","closed_by":{"login":"rayamazaky","id":238893411,"node_id":"U_kgDODj05Yw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238893411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky","html_url":"https://github.com/rayamazaky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c